你可以跟随他们，因为我们现在与办公室女士进行了大量的异花授粉。

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:48.829
But you know what, how does it feel to be on one of the greatest shows of all time?
但你知道吗，参加有史以来最伟大的演出之一感觉如何？

00:04:48.829 --> 00:04:49.910
It feels really good.
感觉真的很好。

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:59.269
And I have a new appreciation for how great the show is since I've been doing this show and I've re-engaged with the show and watched it anew.
自从我开始做这个节目以来，我对这个节目的伟大有了新的认识，并且我重新参与了这个节目并重新观看了它。

00:04:59.269 --> 00:05:25.647
watching it with my wife who's never seen it and it's just been a blast and I'm delighted to now in a weird way become a fan of the show before I was really you know I was on it and I liked it and I appreciated it but I didn't understand on some level the enthusiasm it inspired in people until I watch it now and I'm like oh yeah I get it I get it.
和我从未看过的妻子一起观看它，这真是太棒了，我很高兴现在以一种奇怪的方式成为这个节目的粉丝，然后我才真正知道我参加了它，我喜欢它，我欣赏它，但我在某种程度上不理解它激发了人们的热情，直到我现在观看它，我就像哦，是的，我明白了，我明白了。

00:05:25.647 --> 00:05:31.240
Are you a fan of anything to the extent that people are fans of this show.
你对任何事物的粉丝是否达到了人们对该节目的粉丝的程度？

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:43.439
Is that another reason, maybe, why that level of fandom is hard for you to feel, is hard for you to understand, because maybe that's not quite your way of interacting with art.
这也许是另一个原因，为什么你很难感受到这种程度的粉丝，你很难理解，因为也许这不完全是你与艺术互动的方式。

00:05:43.439 --> 00:05:47.079
You know, I've done a few comic-ons.
你知道，我画过几部漫画。

00:05:47.079 --> 00:05:49.800
I did want an Ecuador last year.
去年我确实想要厄瓜多尔。

00:05:49.800 --> 00:06:02.399
And I'm always touched by the enthusiasm of fans and their excitement to meet the people that they've watched and loved on screen.
我总是被粉丝们的热情以及他们在银幕上见到他们所看过和喜爱的人们的兴奋所感动。

00:06:02.399 --> 00:06:10.680
But I'm more like on the other side of things, like I'm more interested when I watch something and love something, because I create things.
但我更像是事物的另一面，就像当我观看某些东西并喜欢某些东西时我更感兴趣，因为我创造了东西。

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.360
I want to figure out how they did it.
我想弄清楚他们是怎么做到的。

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:14.800
Like I want to look under the hood of the art.
就像我想探究艺术的本质一样。

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:20.800
Like if I love a song, I look up the chords, I figure out why the song is so affecting.
就像如果我喜欢一首歌，我会查找和弦，我会弄清楚为什么这首歌如此感人。

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:23.480
So because I want to write my own songs, you know what I mean?
因为我想写自己的歌，你知道我的意思吗？

00:06:24.879 --> 00:06:39.519
But I think, you know, when I was younger, there were certainly things that I was really, really in love with, but I've always thought of myself more as a creator than a fan, but to be a creator, you have to, of course, love things very deeply.
但我想，你知道，当我年轻的时候，肯定有一些东西是我非常非常喜欢的，但我一直认为自己更像是一个创造者而不是粉丝，但要成为一个创造者，你当然必须非常热爱事物。

00:06:39.519 --> 00:06:47.519
So there are many things that I love, but not in the way that I would dress up and go to come and home as the character.
所以有很多东西是我喜欢的，但不是我像角色那样打扮、回家的方式。

00:06:47.519 --> 00:06:48.519
Right.
正确的。

00:06:48.519 --> 00:06:49.519
Yeah.
是的。

00:06:49.519 --> 00:07:03.217
Well, you know, we've got a lot of questions coming in right now, and there are some people for whom this might be the first time they have seen you do the show live because we used to show the video for the show.
嗯，你知道，我们现在收到了很多问题，对于有些人来说，这可能是他们第一次看到你现场表演，因为我们曾经播放过该节目的视频。

00:07:03.217 --> 00:07:05.210
We don't quite as much anymore.
我们不再那么多了。

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:08.876
And we do have a couple of people pointing something out.
我们确实有几个人指出了一些事情。

00:07:08.876 --> 00:07:11.898
Maybe you can tell Roxy underscore Musking Gum.
也许你可以告诉 Roxy 在麝香口香糖下划线。

00:07:11.898 --> 00:07:16.850
The answer to is that the real blue French horn on your bookshelf behind you.
答案是你身后书架上真正的蓝色圆号。

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:17.959
Yeah, that's it.
是的，就是这样。

00:07:17.959 --> 00:07:51.589
That's the one we all got to take things from set and I think you know, some people took the jukebox or the table, you know, the bar table and I just asked for the blue French horn it felt like the best prop for me to take, you know, yeah I used to be worried that if how I met your mother fans knew that I had it that they would break into my apartment and steal it But I've let that go, but please don't is please don't We have a question here from, I'm trying to get this name here.
这是我们所有人都必须从片场拿走东西的那个，我想你知道，有些人拿走了自动点唱机或桌子，你知道，吧台，我只是要了蓝色圆号，它感觉对我来说是最好的道具，你知道，是的，我曾经担心，如果我遇见你母亲的粉丝知道我有它，他们会闯入我的公寓并偷走它，但我已经放弃了，但请不要这样做，我们有一个问题，我是试图在这里得到这个名字。

00:07:51.589 --> 00:08:03.110
Ellie Rosen-Denn, who's a fan of much of your work, and asks, what do you prefer, acting, music, or directing?
艾莉·罗森-丹恩 (Ellie Rosen-Denn) 是你大部分作品的粉丝，她问，你更喜欢什么，表演、音乐还是导演？

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:04.110
Oh, I don't know.
哦，我不知道。

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:06.069
I was just talking with my wife about this this morning.
今天早上我刚刚和我妻子谈论了这件事。

00:08:06.069 --> 00:08:20.560
I mean, I think in some ways, like, if you wanna know what's really kind of sitting on my heart or what I've been chewing on or what concerns me in the world, listen to my music.
我的意思是，我认为在某些方面，如果你想知道我心里真正想的是什么，或者我一直在咀嚼什么，或者世界上有什么与我有关，那就听听我的音乐。

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:27.319
I think I'm capturing the purest essence of what I'm about and what I'm trying to say in my songs.
我认为我正在捕捉我所想表达的最纯粹的本质以及我在歌曲中想要表达的内容。

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:39.710
And yeah, and I find myself, I don't know, I really only act when something really strikes me as I have to do that.
是的，我发现自己，我不知道，我真的只有在某些事情真正触动我时才会采取行动，因为我必须这样做。

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:45.549
I don't think of it as a must get an acting, you know, when I was in my 20s, it was like, must get an acting job, must get an acting job.
我不认为演戏是必须的，你知道，当我20多岁的时候，就好像，必须得到一份演艺工作，必须得到一份演艺工作。

00:08:45.549 --> 00:08:46.990
And I don't think like that anymore.
我不再那样想了。

00:08:46.990 --> 00:09:05.909
I'm going to do a play in London this summer that I really love, but I like being the conductor and the composer a little more than being the first violinist these days, but I love them all still.
今年夏天我将在伦敦演出一部我非常喜欢的戏剧，但我现在更喜欢担任指挥和作曲家，而不是担任第一小提琴手，但我仍然喜欢他们。

00:09:05.909 --> 00:09:11.549
I mean, when I get a great part to act, I still love it, but I love it in a different way.
我的意思是，当我扮演一个重要的角色时，我仍然喜欢它，但我以不同的方式喜欢它。

00:09:11.549 --> 00:09:14.830
I don't love it in a way that it was the oxygen that I need to breathe.
我不喜欢它，因为它是我呼吸所需的氧气。

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:19.009
That's how it used to feel.
以前就是这样的感觉。

00:09:19.009 --> 00:09:28.960
I wrote you this little day to sing to you in New York City.
今天我写信给你，是为了在纽约为你唱歌。

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:38.450
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:40.610
And now back to the show.
现在回到节目。

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:52.470
Matthias Zaca asks the question that you are definitely well equipped to answer, which is how do you get into show business from the East Coast?
马蒂亚斯·扎卡（Matthias Zaca）问了一个你绝对有能力回答的问题，那就是你是如何从东海岸进入演艺界的？

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:53.549
How do I get into the show?
我如何进入演出？

00:09:53.549 --> 00:09:55.309
How did I?
我怎么了？

00:09:55.309 --> 00:10:00.070
Oh well, how does one, I think he's interested for himself if you're not living in Los Angeles?
哦，好吧，如果你不住在洛杉矶，我想他会对自己感兴趣吗？

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:01.610
Oh, from the East Coast.
哦，来自东海岸。

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:03.269
Okay, well, I'm from Ohio.
好吧，我来自俄亥俄州。

00:10:03.269 --> 00:10:10.309
I mean, I'm actually from Ohio, so it was Ted, but I'm from Columbus, so it's totally different than Cleveland.
我的意思是，我实际上来自俄亥俄州，所以是特德，但我来自哥伦布，所以它与克利夫兰完全不同。

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:13.029
How do you get into show business?
你是如何进入演艺圈的？

00:10:13.029 --> 00:10:18.889
I mean, look, I got out of drama school in 1999 and it was a much different world.
我的意思是，你看，我 1999 年从戏剧学校毕业，那是一个截然不同的世界。

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:28.539
I think one of the benefits of the moment we're in right now is everyone has a phone.
我认为我们现在所处的好处之一是每个人都有一部手机。

00:10:28.539 --> 00:10:31.620
It's got a video component to it.
它有一个视频组件。

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:33.500
You can edit these videos.
您可以编辑这些视频。

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:37.019
You can throw them up on multiple platforms.
您可以将它们放到多个平台上。

00:10:37.019 --> 00:10:44.940
It's so much easier to create your own content and get noticed and actually refine your style and figure out what your style is.
创建自己的内容并获得关注并真正完善您的风格并找出您的风格要容易得多。

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:54.980
I was just reading something that all these people are making horror films that they're putting up on YouTube and Hollywood is kind of like, that's where they're finding the new crop of like great horror directors.
我刚刚读到一些东西，所有这些人都在制作恐怖电影，他们把它们放在 YouTube 上，好莱坞就像是，他们在那里找到了新一批伟大的恐怖导演。

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:57.970
There's nothing better than proof of concept.
没有什么比概念验证更好的了。

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:13.850
You know, if you can show, you can go in a room and pitch a story, but if you show them the movie that you make and you show them, you've got real chops and you know how to scare people or do whatever it is you're trying to do, that's gonna be a lot better than trying to talk your way into something.
你知道，如果你能展示，你可以走进一个房间并讲述一个故事，但如果你向他们展示你制作的电影并向他们展示，你就有了真正的能力，你知道如何吓唬人们或做任何你想做的事情，这比试图通过谈话来实现某件事要好得多。

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:17.409
So just make things, you know, make things, get your friends together.
所以，只要创造一些东西，你知道，创造一些东西，让你的朋友聚在一起。

00:11:17.409 --> 00:11:22.769
The barrier to entry is lower than ever before, the cost is lower, it keeps getting lower and lower.
